    SecretsData: []
    Narration: "<narrations><narration id = \"0\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"
      title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent
      = \"\"><languages><ca>Cases de l'Edat del Bronze</ca><en>BRONZE AGE HOMES</en><es>Hogares
      de la Edad de Bronce</es><fr>Maisons de l'\xE2ge du bronze</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Imagina un poble amb cases
      apretades l\u2019una al costat de l\u2019altra, com peces d\u2019un trencaclosques!
      Aix\xF2 \xE9s el que semblaven les cases d\u2019El Barranc de G\xE0fols, fa
      molts i molts anys.</ca><en>Imagine a village with houses squeezed right next
      to each other, like puzzle pieces! That's what the houses at El Barranc de
      G\xE0fols looked like, many, many years ago. </en><es>Imagina un pueblo con
      casas apretadas justo una al lado de la otra, \xA1como piezas de un rompecabezas!
      As\xED era como se ve\xEDan las casas en El Barranc de G\xE0fols hace much\xEDsimos
      a\xF1os.</es><fr>Imaginez un village o\xF9 les maisons sont serr\xE9es les
      unes contre les autres, comme des pi\xE8ces de puzzle ! C\u2019\xE9tait \xE0
      quoi ressemblaient les maisons \xE0 El Barranc de G\xE0fols, il y a de tr\xE8s,
      tr\xE8s nombreuses ann\xE9es.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>9.528</en><es>10.944</es><fr>10.464</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Eren estrets i llargs,
      com passadissos, amb una base de pedra i parets de tovot. El sostre tamb\xE9
      era de fang i joncs, i gaireb\xE9 pla!</ca><en>They were narrow and long, like
      hallways, with a stone base and mud-brick walls. The roof was also made of
      mud and reeds, and almost flat! </en><es>Eran estrechos y largos, como pasillos,
      con una base de piedra y muros de adobe. El techo tambi\xE9n estaba hecho de
      barro y ca\xF1as, \xA1y casi plano!</es><fr>Ils \xE9taient \xE9troits et longs,
      comme des couloirs, avec une base en pierre et des murs en briques de boue.
      Le toit \xE9tait aussi fait de boue et de roseaux, et presque plat !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>10.015</en><es>9.312</es><fr>9.048</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"LifeBronzeAge\" position = \"2.966581,0.2998015,2.075098\" rotation
      = \"0.04002391,0.07317726,-0.002939094,0.9965112\" scale = \"3.46487,3.46487,3.46487\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"3.698979,-0.3769956,1.227157\"
      rotation = \"0.3280341,0.5597816,-0.2562884,0.7164876\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>A dins, van pintar les parets amb un color
      marr\xF3 ataronjat. All\xE0 guardaven els seus atuells i recipients de fang
      per cuinar i menjar.</ca><en>Inside, they painted the walls an orange-brown
      color. That's where they kept their pots and clay vessels for cooking and eating.</en><es>Por
      dentro, pintaron las paredes de un color marr\xF3n anaranjado. Ah\xED guardaban
      sus ollas y recipientes de barro para cocinar y comer.</es><fr>\xC0 l\u2019int\xE9rieur,
      ils ont peint les murs d\u2019une couleur orange-brun. C\u2019est l\xE0 qu\u2019ils
      conservaient leurs pots et leurs r\xE9cipients en argile pour cuisiner et manger.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>6.624</en><es>7.44</es><fr>8.544</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"3.337508,-0.3815382,0.2425447\" rotation =
      \"0.3419064,0.5258603,-0.2429816,0.7399533\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"1\" startEvent
      = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>DE BRONZE A FERRO</ca><en>FROM
      BRONZE TO IRON</en><es>DE BRONCE A HIERRO</es><fr>De Bronze \xE0 Fer</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molt de temps, la gent
      va comen\xE7ar a utilitzar un metall anomenat bronze. Per\xF2 era tan dif\xEDcil
      d\u2019aconseguir que nom\xE9s les persones m\xE9s riques en podien tenir.</ca><en>A
      very long time ago, people started using a metal called bronze. But it was
      so hard to get that only the richest people could have it. </en><es>Hace mucho,
      mucho tiempo, la gente empez\xF3 a usar un metal llamado bronce. Pero era tan
      dif\xEDcil de conseguir que solo las personas m\xE1s ricas pod\xEDan tenerlo.</es><fr>Il
      y a tr\xE8s longtemps, les gens ont commenc\xE9 \xE0 utiliser un m\xE9tal appel\xE9
      le bronze. Mais il \xE9tait si difficile \xE0 obtenir que seuls les plus riches
      pouvaient en avoir.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>7.056</en><es>8.688</es><fr>8.376</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Despr\xE9s van descobrir
      el ferro, i tot va canviar! El ferro era m\xE9s f\xE0cil de trobar i m\xE9s
      resistent. Gr\xE0cies a ell, la gent podia fabricar eines i armes per a tothom,
      no nom\xE9s per a uns quants. D\u2019aquesta manera, els pagesos tamb\xE9 podien
      tenir bones eines per treballar la terra!</ca><en>Then they discovered iron,
      and everything changed! Iron was easier to find and stronger. With it, people
      could make tools and weapons for everyone, not just for a few. That way, farmers
      could also have good tools to work the land!</en><es>Entonces descubrieron
      el hierro y \xA1todo cambi\xF3! El hierro era m\xE1s f\xE1cil de encontrar
      y m\xE1s resistente. Con \xE9l, la gente pod\xEDa fabricar herramientas y armas
      para todos, no solo para unos pocos. \xA1As\xED, los agricultores tambi\xE9n
      pod\xEDan tener buenas herramientas para trabajar la tierra!</es><fr>Puis ils
      d\xE9couvrirent le fer, et tout changea ! Le fer \xE9tait plus facile \xE0
      trouver et plus solide. Gr\xE2ce \xE0 lui, les gens pouvaient fabriquer des
      outils et des armes pour tous, et pas seulement pour quelques-uns. Ainsi, les
      agriculteurs pouvaient aussi avoir de bons outils pour travailler la terre
      !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>13.68</en><es>16.92</es><fr>15.6</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"ToolsBronze\" position = \"-0.2959589,0.5053335,2.515289\" rotation
      = \"0.01057711,0.9837651,0.06189333,-0.1681181\" scale = \"3.465945,3.465945,3.465945\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"0.05851394,-0.3096198,3.306754\"
      rotation = \"-0.1691589,0.8265702,-0.3306047,-0.4229272\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id =
      \"2\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\"
      audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>EL TRESOR
      DE LLAVORS\xCD</ca><en>THE LLAVORS\xCD HOARD</en><es>EL TESORO DE LLAVORS\xCD</es><fr>LE
      TR\xC9SOR DES LLAVORS\xCD</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>El 1985, alg\xFA va trobar
      un tresor amagat enterrat entre roques a prop de Llavors\xED: 148 objectes
      de bronze!</ca><en>In 1985, someone found a hidden treasure buried among rocks
      near Llavors\xED: 148 bronze objects! </en><es>En 1985, alguien encontr\xF3
      un tesoro oculto enterrado entre rocas cerca de Llavors\xED: \xA1148 objetos
      de bronce!</es><fr>En 1985, quelqu\u2019un a trouv\xE9 un tr\xE9sor cach\xE9
      enfoui parmi des rochers pr\xE8s de Llavors\xED : 148 objets en bronze !</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>8.328</en><es>8.712</es><fr>8.04</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Blacksmith_01\" position = \"-1.771167,0.02666571,4.37816\" rotation
      = \"0.1218685,-0.003509772,0.0004309456,0.99254\" scale = \"0.4616561,0.4616561,0.4616561\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/><asset name = \"Blacksmith_02\"
      position = \"-1.975468,0.02468568,2.19261\" rotation = \"-0.0164996,0.9815306,-0.09970021,-0.1624356\"
      scale = \"0.458865,0.458865,0.458865\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Per qu\xE8 estaven amagats?
      El bronze era molt valu\xF3s, aix\xED que els experts creuen que alg\xFA el
      va amagar expressament, planificant tornar-hi m\xE9s tard. </ca><en>Why were
      they hidden? Bronze was very valuable, so experts believe someone hid it on
      purpose, planning to come back for it later. </en><es>\xBFPor qu\xE9 estaban
      ocultos? El bronce era muy valioso, por lo que los expertos creen que alguien
      lo escondi\xF3 a prop\xF3sito, planeando volver m\xE1s tarde.</es><fr>Pourquoi
      \xE9taient-ils cach\xE9s ? Le bronze \xE9tait tr\xE8s pr\xE9cieux, alors des
      experts pensent que quelqu\u2019un l\u2019a cach\xE9 intentionnellement, en
      pr\xE9voyant d\u2019y revenir plus tard.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for
      language (ca)</ca><en>7.392</en><es>8.592</es><fr>8.688</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Per\xF2 sembla que no
      hi van tornar mai per recuperar-ho!</ca><en>But it seems they never returned
      to get it!</en><es>Pero parece que nunca volvieron a buscarlo.</es><fr>Mais
      il semble qu\u2019ils ne soient jamais revenus le r\xE9cup\xE9rer !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>2.544</en><es>2.496</es><fr>4.152</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Rings\" position = \"-2.768711,0.6306664,3.229929\" rotation = \"-0.04974786,-0.6089492,-0.03831181,0.7907201\"
      scale = \"3.465647,3.465647,3.465647\" type = \"Video\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration
      id = \"3\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>EMP\xDARIES,
      UNA COL\xD2NIA GREGa</ca><en>EMP\xDARIES, A GREEK COLONY</en><es>EMP\xDARIES,
      UNA COLONIA GRIEGA</es><fr>EMP\xDARIES, UNE COLONIE GRECQUE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molts segles, els mariners
      grecs van arribar en vaixell des de lluny i van fundar una ciutat vora el mar:
      Emp\xFAries.</ca><en>Many centuries ago, Greek sailors arrived by boat from
      far away and founded a city by the sea: Emp\xFAries. </en><es>Hace muchos siglos,
      los marineros griegos llegaron en barco desde muy lejos y fundaron una ciudad
      junto al mar: Emp\xFAries.</es><fr>Il y a de nombreux si\xE8cles, des marins
      grecs arriv\xE8rent par bateau de tr\xE8s loin et fond\xE8rent une ville au
      bord de la mer : Emp\xFAries.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>7.2</en><es>7.776</es><fr>7.44</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>El seu nom significa \xABmercat\xBB
      en grec, perqu\xE8 era un lloc on els vaixells venien d\u2019arreu per comprar
      i vendre coses.</ca><en>Its name means \"market\" in Greek, because it was
      a place where ships came from everywhere to buy and sell things. </en><es>Su
      nombre significa \u201Cmercado\u201D en griego, porque era un lugar al que
      llegaban barcos de todas partes para comprar y vender cosas.</es><fr>Son nom
      signifie \xAB march\xE9 \xBB en grec, parce que c\u2019\xE9tait un endroit
      o\xF9 des navires venaient de partout pour acheter et vendre des choses.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>6.624</en><es>7.2</es><fr>6.624</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"RuinasEmpuries\" position = \"-4.782421,0.3590564,2.032661\" rotation
      = \"0.0001555512,0.999545,-0.005233688,0.02970762\" scale = \"3.464303,3.464303,3.464303\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-5.883521,-0.6380843,2.615325\"
      rotation = \"-0.0788959,0.9204344,-0.2518028,-0.2883943\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Emp\xFAries es va convertir en una ciutat
      important i va ajudar la poblaci\xF3 local a descobrir noves idees, objectes
      i costums de terres llunyanes.</ca><en>Emp\xFAries became an important city
      and helped local people discover new ideas, objects, and customs from faraway
      lands.</en><es>Emp\xFAries se convirti\xF3 en una ciudad importante y ayud\xF3
      a la poblaci\xF3n local a descubrir nuevas ideas, objetos y costumbres de tierras
      lejanas.</es><fr>Emp\xFAries est devenue une ville importante et a aid\xE9
      la population locale \xE0 d\xE9couvrir de nouvelles id\xE9es, de nouveaux objets
      et de nouvelles coutumes venus de contr\xE9es lointaines.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>8.328</en><es>8.376</es><fr>10.68</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-6.691518,-0.5092719,3.966305\" rotation =
      \"0.1586171,-0.7003711,0.1642709,0.6762662\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"4\" startEvent
      = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>UNA CULTURA MEDITERR\xC0NIA</ca><en>A
      MEDITERRANEAN CULTURE</en><es>UNA CULTURA MEDITERR\xC1NEA</es><fr>UNE CULTURE
      M\xC9DITERRAN\xC9ENNE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Els ibers, el poble que
      vivia aqu\xED fa molts segles, no estaven sols: comerciaven amb altres pobles
      al voltant de la Mediterr\xE0nia.</ca><en>The Iberians, the people who lived
      here many centuries ago, weren't alone: they traded with other peoples around
      the Mediterranean. </en><es>Los iberos, la gente que vivi\xF3 aqu\xED hace
      muchos siglos, no estaban solos: comerciaban con otros pueblos alrededor del
      Mediterr\xE1neo.</es><fr>Les Ib\xE8res, le peuple qui vivait ici il y a de
      nombreux si\xE8cles, n\u2019\xE9taient pas seuls : ils commer\xE7aient avec
      d\u2019autres peuples autour de la M\xE9diterran\xE9e.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>6.864</en><es>8.04</es><fr>8.208</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Els productes venien del
      nord d\u2019\xC0frica a trav\xE9s d\u2019Eivissa. La cer\xE0mica preciosa venia
      de Gr\xE8cia.</ca><en>Products came from North Africa through Ibiza. Beautiful
      pottery came from Greece. </en><es>Los productos llegaron del norte de \xC1frica
      a trav\xE9s de Ibiza. La hermosa cer\xE1mica lleg\xF3 de Grecia.</es><fr>Les
      produits venaient d\u2019Afrique du Nord via Ibiza. Une belle poterie venait
      de Gr\xE8ce.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>4.872</en><es>6.408</es><fr>5.208</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Anfora\" position = \"-0.859252,0.2613881,11.27649\" rotation = \"0.02966494,-0.008737096,0.0002593095,0.9995217\"
      scale = \"3.466139,3.466139,3.466139\" type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"0.026757,-0.8236305,10.63194\" rotation =
      \"0.3048611,0.2629707,-0.0879888,0.9111335\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\" pause
      = \"False\"><languages><ca>Els pobles que vivien a prop del mar tenien m\xE9s
      contacte amb aquests visitants i creixien m\xE9s r\xE0pidament, mentre que
      els que vivien a l\u2019interior s\u2019centraven sobretot en el conreu i la
      cria d\u2019animals.</ca><en>The peoples who lived near the sea had more contact
      with these visitors and grew faster, while those inland mainly focused on farming
      and raising animals.</en><es>Los pueblos que viv\xEDan cerca del mar ten\xEDan
      m\xE1s contacto con estos visitantes y crec\xEDan m\xE1s r\xE1pido, mientras
      que los del interior se centraban principalmente en la agricultura y la cr\xEDa
      de animales.</es><fr>Les peuples qui vivaient pr\xE8s de la mer avaient plus
      de contacts avec ces visiteurs et grandissaient plus rapidement, tandis que
      ceux vivant \xE0 l\u2019int\xE9rieur des terres se consacraient principalement
      \xE0 l\u2019agriculture et \xE0 l\u2019\xE9levage d\u2019animaux.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>8.088</en><es>11.112</es><fr>11.88</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-1.722066,-0.7899158,10.63139\" rotation =
      \"0.2942372,-0.2750557,0.08884063,0.9109754\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type
      = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"5\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>MOLINS ROTATORIS</ca><en>ROTARY
      MILLS</en><es>MOLINOS ROTATORIOS</es><fr>MOULINS ROTATIFS</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Saps com es feia la farina
      fa milers d\u2019anys? Amb molta feina dura! Al principi, la gent triturava
      el gra a m\xE0, poc a poc.</ca><en>Do you know how flour was made thousands
      of years ago? With a lot of hard work! At first, people ground grain by hand,
      little by little. </en><es>\xBFSabes c\xF3mo se hac\xEDa la harina hace miles
      de a\xF1os? \xA1Con mucho trabajo duro! Al principio, la gente mol\xEDa el
      grano a mano, poco a poco.</es><fr>Savez-vous comment on fabriquait la farine
      il y a des milliers d\u2019ann\xE9es ? Avec beaucoup de travail acharn\xE9
      ! Au d\xE9but, les gens broyaient le grain \xE0 la main, petit \xE0 petit.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>8.808</en><es>8.328</es><fr>8.976</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Carpenter\" position = \"0.9596153,0.1224091,10.24739\" rotation =
      \"-0.001688835,0.9975739,-0.06451015,-0.02611585\" scale = \"0.5461183,0.5461183,0.5461183\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token id = \"1\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Per\xF2 fa molts segles, els ibers van inventar
      un mol\xED que feia aix\xF2: abocaves el gra per un forat a la part superior
      i, mentre la pedra girava, aixafava el gra fins a convertir-lo en farina.</ca><en>But
      many centuries ago, the Iberians invented a mill that turned: you poured grain
      through a hole on top, and as the stone spun, it crushed the grain into flour.</en><es>Pero
      hace muchos siglos, los \xEDberos inventaron un molino que convert\xEDa: vert\xEDas
      el grano a trav\xE9s de un orificio en la parte superior y, mientras la piedra
      giraba, trituraba el grano hasta convertirlo en harina.</es><fr>Mais il y a
      de cela de nombreux si\xE8cles, les Ib\xE8res ont invent\xE9 un moulin qui
      fonctionnait ainsi : vous versiez le grain par un trou situ\xE9 en haut, et,
      tandis que la pierre tournait, elle broyait le grain en farine.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>10.176</en><es>12.144</es><fr>11.976</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"MolinoGris,MolinoOlson\" position = \"1.942974,0.4777002,11.35573\"
      rotation = \"-0.01675617,0.727554,0.01778113,0.6856152\" scale = \"3.464379,3.464379,3.464379\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\" pause
      = \"False\"><languages><ca>Una invenci\xF3 brillant que va fer la feina molt
      m\xE9s f\xE0cil!</ca><en>A brilliant invention that made the work much easier!</en><es>\xA1Una
      brillante invenci\xF3n que hizo el trabajo mucho m\xE1s f\xE1cil!</es><fr>Une
      invention brillante qui a rendu le travail beaucoup plus facile !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>2.952</en><es>4.042</es><fr>3.96</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"6\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>UN
      PETIT VAIXELL ROM\xC0</ca><en>A SMALL ROMAN SHIP</en><es>UN PEQUE\xD1O BARCO
      ROMANO</es><fr>UN PETIT NAVIRE ROMAIN</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>M\xE9s de dos mil anys
      enrere, un vaixell rom\xE0 anomenat Culip IV navegava a prop del cap de Creus
      quan es va enfonsar. Era un vaixell min\xFAscul, m\xE9s curt que una piscina
      ol\xEDmpica!</ca><en>More than two thousand years ago, a Roman ship called
      Culip IV was sailing near Cape Creus when it sank. It was a tiny ship, shorter
      than an Olympic swimming pool! </en><es>M\xE1s de dos mil a\xF1os atr\xE1s,
      un barco romano llamado Culip IV navegaba cerca del cabo de Creus cuando se
      hundi\xF3. \xA1Era un barco diminuto, m\xE1s corto que una piscina ol\xEDmpica!</es><fr>Il
      y a plus de deux mille ans, un navire romain appel\xE9 Culip IV naviguait pr\xE8s
      du cap de Creus lorsqu\u2019il a coul\xE9. C\u2019\xE9tait un tout petit navire,
      plus court qu\u2019une piscine olympique !</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>10.056</en><es>11.04</es><fr>10.896</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Merchant_01\" position = \"3.688454,0.8094716,8.249096\" rotation
      = \"-0.1079199,0.03816688,0.004146259,0.993418\" scale = \"0.6008493,0.6008493,0.6008493\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Talking\"/><asset name = \"Merchant_02\" position
      = \"4.500345,0.7821566,8.008343\" rotation = \"-0.09774859,0.2524615,0.02564414,0.9623153\"
      scale = \"0.6058975,0.6058975,0.6058975\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Portava tresors: \xE0mfores
      plenes d\u2019oli, plaques de fang, fanals d\u2019oli per a la llum i fins
      i tot vi!</ca><en>It was carrying treasures: amphorae full of oil, clay plates,
      oil lamps for light, and even wine!</en><es>Llevaba tesoros: \xE1nforas llenas
      de aceite, platos de arcilla, l\xE1mparas de aceite para la luz e incluso \xA1vino!</es><fr>Il
      transportait des tr\xE9sors : des amphores pleines d\u2019huile, des plaques
      d\u2019argile, des lampes \xE0 huile pour s\u2019\xE9clairer, et m\xEAme du
      vin !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>7.488</en><es>7.92</es><fr>7.32</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Gr\xE0cies a tot el que
      portava, avui sabem com viatjaven els vaixells i qu\xE8 transportaven en aquell
      temps.</ca><en>Thanks to everything it was carrying, today we know how ships
      traveled and what they transported back then.</en><es>Gracias a todo lo que
      llevaba, hoy sabemos c\xF3mo viajaban los barcos y qu\xE9 transportaban en
      aquel entonces.</es><fr>Gr\xE2ce \xE0 tout ce qu\u2019elles transportaient,
      aujourd\u2019hui, nous savons comment les navires voyageaient et ce qu\u2019ils
      ramenaient \xE0 cette \xE9poque.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language
      (ca)</ca><en>5.304</en><es>6.024</es><fr>6.984</fr></audios></token></narration></narrations>"
