    SecretsData: []
    Narration: "<narrations><narration id = \"0\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"
      title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent
      = \"\"><languages><ca>ROM\xC0NIC: UNA NOVA LLENGUA</ca><en>ROMANESQUE: A NEW
      LANGUAGE</en><es>ROM\xC1NICO: UN NUEVO IDIOMA</es><fr>ROMANESQUE : UNE NOUVELLE
      LANGUE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molts i molts anys,
      va comen\xE7ar a construir-se a Catalunya un nou tipus d\u2019esgl\xE9sia i
      d\u2019edifici: l\u2019estil rom\xE0nic! Un home important anomenat l\u2019abat
      Oliba va ajudar a fer que aquest estil es fes molt popular.</ca><en>Many, many
      years ago, a new type of church and building started being built in Catalonia:
      the Romanesque style! An important man named Abbot Oliba helped make this style
      very popular. </en><es>Hace muchos, muchos a\xF1os, empez\xF3 a construirse
      en Catalu\xF1a un nuevo tipo de iglesia y de edificio: \xA1el estilo rom\xE1nico!
      Un hombre importante llamado el abad Oliba ayud\xF3 a que este estilo se hiciera
      muy popular.</es><fr>Il y a de nombreuses ann\xE9es, un nouveau type d\u2019\xE9glise
      et de b\xE2timent a commenc\xE9 \xE0 \xEAtre construit en Catalogne : le style
      roman ! Un homme important nomm\xE9 l\u2019abb\xE9 Oliba a contribu\xE9 \xE0
      rendre ce style tr\xE8s populaire.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>11.448</en><es>12.264</es><fr>12.168</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Podeu recon\xE8ixer les
      esgl\xE9sies rom\xE0niques perqu\xE8 tenen formes arrodonides, com ara mitja
      circumfer\xE8ncia, i murs decorats amb petites arcades.</ca><en>You can recognize
      Romanesque churches because they have rounded shapes, like half a circle, and
      walls decorated with little arches. </en><es>Puedes reconocer las iglesias
      rom\xE1nicas porque tienen formas redondeadas, como un semic\xEDrculo, y muros
      decorados con peque\xF1os arcos.</es><fr>Vous pouvez reconna\xEEtre les \xE9glises
      romanes parce qu\u2019elles ont des formes arrondies, comme un demi-cercle,
      et des murs d\xE9cor\xE9s de petites arcades.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>7.488</en><es>6.96</es><fr>7.656</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"newchurch\" position = \"4.102995,0.1501265,-0.6395048\" rotation
      = \"0.04949632,0.5096989,-0.02938897,0.858425\" scale = \"3.465623,3.465623,3.465623\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"3.891523,-0.7899132,-1.694026\"
      rotation = \"0.183253,0.7639574,-0.246751,0.5673635\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Les esgl\xE9sies no eren l\u2019\xFAnic que
      es va construir d\u2019aquesta manera: tamb\xE9 es van construir castells i
      altres edificis, i a m\xE9s es van fer pintures i escultures amb aquest mateix
      estil!</ca><en>Churches weren't the only thing built like this \u2014 castles
      and other buildings were too, and paintings and sculptures were made in this
      style as well!</en><es>Las iglesias no fueron lo \xFAnico que se construy\xF3
      de esta manera: tambi\xE9n se construyeron castillos y otros edificios, \xA1y
      hasta se hicieron pinturas y esculturas con este estilo!</es><fr>Les \xE9glises
      n\u2019\xE9taient pas les seules choses construites comme \xE7a : des ch\xE2teaux
      et d\u2019autres b\xE2timents l\u2019\xE9taient aussi, et des peintures et
      des sculptures \xE9taient r\xE9alis\xE9es dans ce style \xE9galement !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>8.208</en><es>9.96</es><fr>9.288</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"1\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>LA
      FEINA DE L\u2019ABAT OLIBA</ca><en>THE WORK OF ABBOT OLIBA</en><es>EL TRABAJO
      DEL ABAD OLIBA</es><fr>LE TRAVAIL DE L\u2019ABB\xC9 OLIBA</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Oliba era un comte, per\xF2
      un dia va decidir deixar-ho tot enrere i convertir-se en monjo! Va anar a viure
      al monestir de Ripoll l\u2019any 1002. Amb el temps, es va convertir en l\u2019abat
      de diversos monestirs i tamb\xE9 en bisbe.</ca><en>Oliba was a count, but one
      day he decided to leave it all behind and become a monk! He went to live at
      the Ripoll monastery in the year 1002. Over time, he became the head of several
      monasteries and also a bishop. </en><es>Oliba era un conde, pero un d\xEDa
      decidi\xF3 dejarlo todo atr\xE1s y \xA1convertirse en monje! Se fue a vivir
      al monasterio de Ripoll en el a\xF1o 1002. Con el paso del tiempo, se convirti\xF3
      en el jefe de varios monasterios y tambi\xE9n en obispo.</es><fr>Oliba \xE9tait
      comte, mais un jour, il d\xE9cida de tout laisser derri\xE8re lui et de devenir
      moine ! Il alla vivre au monast\xE8re de Ripoll en l\u2019an 1002. Au fil du
      temps, il devint \xE0 la t\xEAte de plusieurs monast\xE8res et aussi \xE9v\xEAque.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>12.6</en><es>12.648</es><fr>12.706</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>L\u2019Oliva va ajudar
      la gent a resoldre els seus problemes i baralles. I tenia una idea brillant!
      L\u2019any 1027, va aconseguir que la gent promet\xE9s no fer guerres en determinats
      dies de la setmana, perqu\xE8 hi pogu\xE9s haver m\xE9s pau.</ca><en>Oliba
      helped people solve their problems and quarrels. And he had a brilliant idea!
      In the year 1027, he got people to promise not to fight wars on certain days
      of the week, so there could be more peace.</en><es>Oliba ayud\xF3 a las personas
      a resolver sus problemas y sus disputas. \xA1Y tuvo una idea brillante! En
      el a\xF1o 1027, logr\xF3 que la gente prometiera no hacer guerras en ciertos
      d\xEDas de la semana, para que pudiera haber m\xE1s paz.</es><fr>Oliba a aid\xE9
      les gens \xE0 r\xE9soudre leurs probl\xE8mes et leurs disputes. Et il avait
      une id\xE9e g\xE9niale ! En 1027, il a fait promettre aux gens de ne pas se
      faire la guerre certains jours de la semaine, afin qu\u2019il y ait davantage
      de paix.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>12.438</en><es>12.528</es><fr>12.312</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"santvicentcardona2\" position = \"11.16996,0.393962,1.399495\" rotation
      = \"-0.002225092,0.7704712,0.002689353,0.6374652\" scale = \"3.466534,3.466534,3.466534\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"10.66524,-0.5279818,0.7520667\"
      rotation = \"0.1078051,0.8624767,-0.2070626,0.4490402\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Aix\xF2 s\u2019anomenava la Pau i la Treva
      de D\xE9u!</ca><en>This was called the Peace and Truce of God!</en><es>\xA1Esto
      se llam\xF3 la Paz y la Tregua de Dios!</es><fr>C\u2019\xE9tait ce qu\u2019on
      appelait la Paix et la Tr\xEAve de Dieu !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>2.544</en><es>3.36</es><fr>3.768</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"2\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>ELS
      CASTELLS</ca><en>THE CASTLES</en><es>LOS CASTILLOS</es><fr>LES CH\xC2TEAUX</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molts segles, Catalunya
      era una regi\xF3 fronterera, aix\xED que la gent va construir castells i torres
      per vigilar. Al principi eren simples, per\xF2 mica en mica els van fer m\xE9s
      forts, amb pedra i murs enormes.</ca><en>Many centuries ago, Catalonia was
      a border region, so people built castles and towers to keep watch. At first
      they were simple, but little by little they made them stronger, with stone
      and huge walls.</en><es>Hace muchos siglos, Catalu\xF1a era una regi\xF3n fronteriza,
      as\xED que la gente construy\xF3 castillos y torres para vigilar. Al principio
      eran sencillos, pero poco a poco los hicieron m\xE1s fuertes, con piedra y
      enormes murallas.</es><fr>Il y a de nombreux si\xE8cles, la Catalogne \xE9tait
      une r\xE9gion frontali\xE8re, alors les gens construisaient des ch\xE2teaux
      et des tours pour surveiller les alentours. Au d\xE9but, ils \xE9taient simples,
      mais peu \xE0 peu, ils les rendirent plus solides, avec de la pierre et de
      gigantesques remparts.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>12.552</en><es>13.08</es><fr>15.048</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Amb el pas del temps,
      hi va haver tants castells que van formar una gran xarxa per protegir tota
      la zona!</ca><en>Over time, there were so many castles that they formed a great
      network protecting the whole area! </en><es>Con el paso del tiempo, hubo tantos
      castillos que formaron una gran red protegiendo toda el \xE1rea.</es><fr>Au
      fil du temps, il y eut tellement de ch\xE2teaux qu\u2019ils form\xE8rent un
      vaste r\xE9seau prot\xE9geant toute la r\xE9gion !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>5.016</en><es>5.952</es><fr>6.072</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"castletower\" position = \"11.09603,0.3660392,2.579208\" rotation
      = \"0.001931479,0.8329166,-0.002907115,0.5533876\" scale = \"3.465686,3.465686,3.465686\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"10.27795,-0.726782,2.041522\"
      rotation = \"0.09409965,0.9051632,-0.2732846,0.3116734\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Per\xF2 els castells no nom\xE9s servien per
      defensar-se dels enemics: tamb\xE9 permetien al senyor del castell governar
      les persones que vivien als voltants.</ca><en>But castles weren't just for
      defending against enemies \u2014 they also let the lord of the castle rule
      over the people who lived nearby.</en><es>Pero los castillos no solo serv\xEDan
      para defenderse de los enemigos; tambi\xE9n permit\xEDan al se\xF1or del castillo
      gobernar a las personas que viv\xEDan cerca.</es><fr>Mais les ch\xE2teaux n\u2019\xE9taient
      pas seulement l\xE0 pour se d\xE9fendre contre les ennemis : ils permettaient
      aussi au seigneur du ch\xE2teau de gouverner les personnes qui vivaient aux
      alentours.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>7.992</en><es>8.088</es><fr>8.76</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"10.32233,-0.8677588,4.493631\" rotation =
      \"0.3073044,0.3474363,-0.1216704,0.877524\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"3\" startEvent
      = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>LA FEUDALITZACI\xD3 DE LA
      SOCIETAT</ca><en>THE FEUDALIZATION OF SOCIETY</en><es>LA FEUDALIZACI\xD3N DE
      LA SOCIEDAD</es><fr>LA FEUDALISATION DE LA SOCI\xC9T\xC9</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molt de temps, els
      nobles m\xE9s poderosos van comen\xE7ar a obtenir cada vegada m\xE9s control
      sobre les terres i sobre les persones que hi vivien. El senyor del castell
      governava tothom al seu territori.</ca><en>A long time ago, the most powerful
      nobles began to gain more and more control over the land and the people who
      lived on it. The lord of the castle ruled over everyone in his territory</en><es>Hace
      mucho tiempo, los nobles m\xE1s poderosos comenzaron a ganar cada vez m\xE1s
      control sobre la tierra y sobre las personas que viv\xEDan en ella. El se\xF1or
      del castillo gobernaba a todos en su territorio</es><fr>Il y a longtemps, les
      plus puissants nobles commenc\xE8rent \xE0 gagner de plus en plus de contr\xF4le
      sur les terres et sur les personnes qui y vivaient. Le seigneur du ch\xE2teau
      r\xE9gnait sur tous ceux qui se trouvaient dans son territoire</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>11.232</en><es>11.928</es><fr>10.992</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>A canvi d\u2019protegir-los,
      els va demanar que treballessin per mantenir i defensar el castell.</ca><en>In
      exchange for protecting them, he asked them to work to maintain and defend
      the castle.</en><es>A cambio de protegerlos, les pidi\xF3 que trabajaran para
      mantener y defender el castillo. </es><fr>En \xE9change de leur protection,
      il leur demanda de travailler pour entretenir et d\xE9fendre le ch\xE2teau.
      </fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>5.28</en><es>5.088</es><fr>5.448</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Totes aquestes normes sobre
      com els senyors i la seva gent s\u2019havien de portar b\xE9 es van escriure
      en un llibre anomenat els Usatges de Barcelona.</ca><en>All these rules for
      how lords and their people should get along were written down in a book called
      the Usatges de Barcelona. </en><es>Todas estas normas sobre c\xF3mo los se\xF1ores
      y su gente deb\xEDan llevarse bien se escribieron en un libro llamado los Usatges
      de Barcelona. </es><fr>Toutes ces r\xE8gles sur la mani\xE8re dont les seigneurs
      et leur peuple devaient s\u2019entendre ont \xE9t\xE9 consign\xE9es dans un
      livre appel\xE9 les Usatges de Barcelone. </fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>7.776</en><es>8.088</es><fr>6.96</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"4\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>UN
      VESTIT COMPLEX</ca><en>A COMPLEX OUTFIT</en><es>UN CONJUNTO COMPLEJO</es><fr>UNE
      TENUE COMPL\xC8XE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Saps quanta equipaci\xF3
      necessitava un cavaller per lluitar? Tant! Portava una camisa feta de petits
      anells de metall per protegir-se, guants especials i un casc al cap.</ca><en>Do
      you know how much gear a knight needed to fight? So much! He wore a shirt made
      of tiny metal rings to protect himself, special gloves, and a helmet on his
      head. </en><es>\xBFSabes cu\xE1nta armadura necesitaba un caballero para pelear?
      \xA1Tanto! Llevaba una camisa hecha de peque\xF1os anillos de metal para protegerse,
      guantes especiales y un casco en la cabeza.</es><fr>Savez-vous de combien d\u2019\xE9quipement
      un chevalier avait besoin pour combattre ? Tellement ! Il portait une chemise
      faite de minuscules anneaux de m\xE9tal pour se prot\xE9ger, des gants sp\xE9ciaux
      et un casque sur la t\xEAte.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>10.464</en><es>10.68</es><fr>11.448</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Com a armes, va utilitzar
      una espasa i una llan\xE7a llarga, amb una petita bandera lligada a la punta.
      Com que tots els cavallers anaven tan coberts, era dif\xEDcil saber qui era
      qui.</ca><en>As weapons, he used a sword and a long lance, with a little flag
      tied to the tip. Since all the knights were covered up so much, it was hard
      to tell who was who. </en><es>Como armas, us\xF3 una espada y una lanza larga,
      con una peque\xF1a bandera atada a la punta. Como todos los caballeros estaban
      tan cubiertos, era dif\xEDcil saber qui\xE9n era qui\xE9n.</es><fr>En guise
      d\u2019armes, il utilisait une \xE9p\xE9e et une longue lance, avec un petit
      drapeau attach\xE9 \xE0 la pointe. Comme tous les chevaliers \xE9taient tellement
      couverts, il \xE9tait difficile de savoir qui \xE9tait qui.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>8.64</en><es>10.728</es><fr>10.896</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Horse\" position = \"4.755947,-0.2463883,6.675032\" rotation = \"0.0006399922,0.999176,-0.0366379,0.01745365\"
      scale = \"1,1,1\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Knight\"
      position = \"5.087508,-0.4845253,5.962938\" rotation = \"0.03645862,-0.7725739,0.04454615,0.63231\"
      scale = \"2.49074,2.49074,2.49074\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Idle\"/><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"5.859481,-0.6857526,5.138264\" rotation =
      \"-0.103876,0.8908299,-0.2571249,-0.3598869\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type
      = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\" pause
      = \"False\"><languages><ca>Aix\xED que van comen\xE7ar a pintar quadres i s\xEDmbols
      especials als seus escuts, perqu\xE8 tothom els pogu\xE9s recon\xE8ixer en
      batalla!</ca><en>So they started painting special pictures and symbols on their
      shields, so everyone could recognize them in battle!</en><es>As\xED que empezaron
      a pintar cuadros especiales y s\xEDmbolos en sus escudos, \xA1para que todos
      pudieran reconocerlos en la batalla!</es><fr>Alors, ils commenc\xE8rent \xE0
      peindre des images et des symboles sp\xE9ciaux sur leurs boucliers, afin que
      chacun puisse les reconna\xEEtre pendant la bataille !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>5.64</en><es>6.936</es><fr>7.392</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"5\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>SANT
      VICEN\xC7 DE CARDONA</ca><en>SANT VICEN\xC7 DE CARDONA</en><es>SAN VICENTE
      DE CARDONA</es><fr>SANT VICEN\xC7 DE CARDONA</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>A dins del castell de
      Cardona hi ha una esgl\xE9sia molt especial anomenada Sant Vicen\xE7. \xC9s
      una de les esgl\xE9sies rom\xE0niques m\xE9s belles de tot Catalunya.</ca><en>Inside
      Cardona Castle there's a very special church called Sant Vicen\xE7. It's one
      of the most beautiful Romanesque churches in all of Catalonia.</en><es>Dentro
      del castillo de Cardona hay una iglesia muy especial llamada Sant Vicen\xE7.
      Es una de las iglesias rom\xE1nicas m\xE1s hermosas de toda Catalu\xF1a.</es><fr>\xC0
      l\u2019int\xE9rieur du ch\xE2teau de Cardona, il y a une \xE9glise tr\xE8s
      sp\xE9ciale appel\xE9e Sant Vicen\xE7. C\u2019est l\u2019une des plus belles
      \xE9glises romanes de toute la Catalogne.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>8.888</en><es>8.088</es><fr>8.688</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Priest_01\" position = \"2.171316,-0.1765259,2.052013\" rotation =
      \"0.008492426,0.9783612,-0.04100571,0.202622\" scale = \"0.1715703,0.1715703,0.1715703\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Arguing\"/><asset name = \"Priest_02\" position
      = \"1.620605,-0.144631,1.762731\" rotation = \"0.007478792,0.9877474,-0.05003734,0.1476329\"
      scale = \"0.1720977,0.1720977,0.1720977\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Talking\"/></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>T\xE9 tres naus a l\u2019interior
      i una c\xFApula rodona al centre. I el m\xE9s curi\xF3s \xE9s que es va construir
      molt r\xE0pidament!</ca><en>It has three aisles inside and a round dome in
      the center. And the most curious thing is that it was built very quickly!</en><es>Tiene
      tres naves en su interior y una c\xFApula redonda en el centro. \xA1Y lo m\xE1s
      curioso es que se construy\xF3 muy r\xE1pidamente!</es><fr>Il y a trois all\xE9es
      \xE0 l\u2019int\xE9rieur et un d\xF4me rond au centre. Et la chose la plus
      curieuse, c\u2019est qu\u2019il a \xE9t\xE9 construit tr\xE8s rapidement !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>6.6</en><es>7.488</es><fr>7.224</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"1.345337,-0.6200001,2.234578\" rotation =
      \"-0.05114343,0.9468799,-0.2537158,-0.1908698\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type
      = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\" pause
      = \"False\"><languages><ca>La construcci\xF3 va comen\xE7ar abans de l\u2019any
      1029 i ja estava acabada el 1040. Per aix\xF2 tot l\u2019edifici t\xE9 un aspecte
      tan uniforme, com si s\u2019hagu\xE9s fet d\u2019una sola vegada!</ca><en>Construction
      started before the year 1029, and it was already finished in 1040. That's why
      the whole building looks so uniform, as if it had been made all at once!</en><es>La
      construcci\xF3n comenz\xF3 antes del a\xF1o 1029 y ya estaba terminada en 1040.
      Por eso todo el edificio tiene un aspecto tan uniforme, \xA1como si se hubiera
      hecho de una sola vez!</es><fr>La construction a commenc\xE9 avant l\u2019ann\xE9e
      1029 et elle \xE9tait d\xE9j\xE0 termin\xE9e en 1040. C\u2019est pourquoi tout
      l\u2019\xE9difice a l\u2019air aussi uniforme, comme s\u2019il avait \xE9t\xE9
      r\xE9alis\xE9 d\u2019un seul coup !</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language
      (ca)</ca><en>10.728</en><es>10.632</es><fr>9.912</fr></audios><asset name =
      \"Monks\" position = \"2.554543,1.037733,0.7913816\" rotation = \"-0.04289029,0.9528295,0.161159,0.2535827\"
      scale = \"3.464832,3.464832,3.464832\" type = \"Video\" animation = \"\"/><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"2.997441,-0.5092702,2.332476\" rotation =
      \"0.06524936,0.9329872,-0.2188302,0.2781921\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type
      = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"6\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>MOLINS DE FARINA</ca><en>FLOUR
      MILLS</en><es>MOLINOS DE HARINA</es><fr>MINOTERIES</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Fa molt de temps, fer
      farina era una feina molt dif\xEDcil i esgotadora. Per\xF2 alg\xFA va tenir
      una idea brillant: utilitzar la for\xE7a de l\u2019aigua del riu per fer girar
      els molins!</ca><en>Long ago, making flour was very hard, tiring work. But
      someone had a brilliant idea: using the power of river water to turn the mills!</en><es>Hace
      mucho tiempo, hacer harina era un trabajo muy dif\xEDcil y agotador. Pero alguien
      tuvo una idea brillante: \xA1usar la fuerza del agua del r\xEDo para mover
      los molinos!</es><fr>Il y a longtemps, fabriquer de la farine \xE9tait un travail
      tr\xE8s difficile et fatigant. Mais quelqu\u2019un a eu une id\xE9e brillante
      : utiliser la puissance de l\u2019eau de la rivi\xE8re pour faire tourner les
      moulins !</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>10.848</en><es>9.408</es><fr>10.608</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>D\u2019aquesta manera,
      la gent ja no havia de treballar tant per moldre el gra. Aquesta invenci\xF3
      es va fer molt popular a Catalunya entre els segles XI i XIII.</ca><en>That
      way, people no longer had to work so hard to grind grain. This invention became
      very popular in Catalonia between the 11th and 13th centuries. </en><es>De
      ese modo, las personas ya no ten\xEDan que trabajar tanto para moler el grano.
      Esta invenci\xF3n se hizo muy popular en Catalu\xF1a entre los siglos XI y
      XIII.</es><fr>Ainsi, les gens n\u2019avaient plus besoin de travailler aussi
      dur pour moudre le grain. Cette invention est devenue tr\xE8s populaire en
      Catalogne entre les XIe et XIIIe si\xE8cles.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>9.912</en><es>9.576</es><fr>9.36</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"molinoagua\" position = \"3.505136,0.2474528,13.42352\" rotation =
      \"0.03196513,0.265357,-0.008802765,0.96358\" scale = \"3.46504,3.46504,3.46504\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"2.265911,-0.3105962,12.76625\"
      rotation = \"0.1745584,-0.09441589,0.01681803,0.9799654\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Dit aix\xF2, els molins pertanyien als senyors
      de la terra, i la gent hi havia d\u2019anar i pagar amb una part de la farina
      que en treia.</ca><en>That said, the mills belonged to the lords of the land,
      and people had to use them and pay with some of the flour they made.</en><es>Dicho
      eso, los molinos pertenec\xEDan a los se\xF1ores de la tierra, y la gente ten\xEDa
      que usarlos y pagar con parte de la harina que produc\xEDa.</es><fr>Cela dit,
      les moulins appartenaient aux seigneurs du pays, et les gens devaient les utiliser
      et leur payer une partie de la farine qu\u2019ils produisaient.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>6.456</en><es>8.256</es><fr>7.32</fr></audios></token></narration></narrations>"
