    Narration: "<narrations><narration id = \"0\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"
      title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent
      = \"\"><languages><ca>Cases de l'Edat del Bronze</ca><en>BRONZE AGE HOMES</en><es>Hogares
      de la Edad de Bronce</es><fr>Maisons de l'\xE2ge du bronze</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>A El Barranc de G\xE0fols,
      al costat del riu Ebre, s\u2019ha conservat un dels assentaments m\xE9s complets
      de finals de l\u2019Edat del Bronze. Els seus carrers s\u2019entrecreuen formant
      angles rectes, i les cases, molt estretes i allargades, comparteixen parets
      entre elles.</ca><en>At El Barranc de G\xE0fols, next to the Ebro river, one
      of the most complete settlements from the late Bronze Age has been preserved.
      Its streets cross at right angles, and the houses, very narrow and elongated,
      share walls with one another. </en><es>En el Barranc de G\xE0fols, junto al
      r\xEDo Ebro, se ha conservado uno de los asentamientos m\xE1s completos de
      la Edad del Bronce tard\xEDa. Sus calles se cruzan en \xE1ngulo recto y las
      casas, muy estrechas y alargadas, comparten muros entre s\xED.</es><fr>\xC0
      el Barranc de G\xE0fols, pr\xE8s de la rivi\xE8re \xC8bre, l\u2019un des \xE9tablissements
      les mieux conserv\xE9s de la fin de l\u2019\xE2ge du Bronze a \xE9t\xE9 pr\xE9serv\xE9.
      Ses rues se croisent \xE0 angle droit et les maisons, tr\xE8s \xE9troites et
      allong\xE9es, partagent leurs murs les unes avec les autres.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>13.896</en><es>14.64</es><fr>14.016</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Van ser constru\xEFts
      amb pedra a la base i murs de tova, coronats amb un sostre gaireb\xE9 pla fet
      de fang i joncs, recolzat sobre bigues de fusta.</ca><en>They were built with
      stone at the base and mud-brick walls, topped with an almost flat roof made
      of mud and reeds resting on wooden beams</en><es>Fueron construidos con piedra
      en la base y muros de adobe, coronados con un techo casi plano hecho de barro
      y juncos, apoyado sobre vigas de madera</es><fr>Ils ont \xE9t\xE9 construits
      avec une base en pierre et des murs en briques de boue, surmont\xE9s d\u2019un
      toit presque plat fait de boue et de roseaux reposant sur des poutres en bois</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>7.776</en><es>9.192</es><fr>9.12</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"3.698979,-0.3769956,1.227157\" rotation =
      \"0.3280341,0.5597816,-0.2562884,0.7164876\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"LifeBronzeAge\" position =
      \"3.115237,0.2544196,2.031408\" rotation = \"0.03128134,0.09058923,-0.002846869,0.9953929\"
      scale = \"3.46487,3.46487,3.46487\" type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>A l\u2019interior, les
      parets estaven arrebossades i pintades d\u2019ocre, i entre les restes s\u2019han
      trobat nombrosos vasos de cer\xE0mica que formaven part de la vida quotidiana
      dels seus habitants.</ca><en>Inside, the walls were plastered and painted ochre,
      and among the remains, numerous ceramic vessels have been found that were part
      of the daily life of their inhabitants</en><es>En el interior, las paredes
      estaban enyesadas y pintadas de color ocre, y entre los restos se han encontrado
      numerosas vasijas de cer\xE1mica que formaban parte de la vida cotidiana de
      sus habitantes</es><fr>\xC0 l\u2019int\xE9rieur, les murs \xE9taient enduits
      et peints en ocre, et parmi les vestiges, de nombreux vases en c\xE9ramique
      ont \xE9t\xE9 retrouv\xE9s, faisant partie de la vie quotidienne de leurs habitants</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>9.84</en><es>11.616</es><fr>10.632</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"3.337508,-0.3815382,0.2425447\" rotation =
      \"0.3419064,0.5258603,-0.2429816,0.7399533\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"1\" startEvent
      = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>DE BRONZE A FERRO</ca><en>FROM
      BRONZE TO IRON</en><es>DE BRONCE A HIERRO</es><fr>De Bronze \xE0 Fer</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Cap al 1700 aC, comen\xE7a
      l\u2019Edat del Bronze en aquesta regi\xF3, tot i que l\u2019\xFAs del metall
      s\u2019est\xE9n molt lentament: era esc\xE0s i dif\xEDcil de treballar, de
      manera que nom\xE9s les fam\xEDlies m\xE9s poderoses podien tenir objectes
      de bronze. Tot canvia amb l\u2019arribada del ferro.</ca><en>Around 1700 BC,
      the Bronze Age begins in this region, though the use of metal spreads very
      slowly: it was scarce and difficult to work, so only the most powerful families
      could own bronze objects. Everything changes with the arrival of iron.</en><es>Alrededor
      de 1700 a. C., comienza la Edad del Bronce en esta regi\xF3n, aunque el uso
      del metal se difunde muy lentamente: era escaso y dif\xEDcil de trabajar, por
      lo que solo las familias m\xE1s poderosas pod\xEDan poseer objetos de bronce.
      Todo cambia con la llegada del hierro.</es><fr>Vers 1700 av. J.-C., l\u2019\xE2ge
      du Bronze commence dans cette r\xE9gion, bien que l\u2019usage du m\xE9tal
      se r\xE9pande tr\xE8s lentement : il \xE9tait rare et difficile \xE0 travailler,
      si bien que seules les familles les plus puissantes pouvaient poss\xE9der des
      objets en bronze. Tout change avec l\u2019arriv\xE9e du fer.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>15.336</en><es>16.224</es><fr>15.456</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Els primers objectes de
      ferro apareixen al voltant de l\u2019any 800 aC, per\xF2 no \xE9s fins al 600
      aC que el seu \xFAs es generalitza. El ferro \xE9s m\xE9s dur i molt m\xE9s
      f\xE0cil d\u2019obtenir que el bronze.</ca><en>The first iron objects appear
      around 800 BC, but it isn't until 600 BC that its use becomes widespread. Iron
      is harder and much easier to obtain than bronze.</en><es>Los primeros objetos
      de hierro aparecen alrededor del 800 a. C., pero no es hasta el 600 a. C. que
      su uso se generaliza. El hierro es m\xE1s duro y mucho m\xE1s f\xE1cil de obtener
      que el bronce.</es><fr>Les premiers objets en fer apparaissent vers 800 av.
      J.-C., mais ce n\u2019est qu\u2019en 600 av. J.-C. que son utilisation se g\xE9n\xE9ralise.
      Le fer est plus dur et beaucoup plus facile \xE0 obtenir que le bronze.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>10.824</en><es>12.888</es><fr>12.144</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"ToolsBronze\" position = \"-0.2959589,0.5053335,2.515289\" rotation
      = \"0.01057711,0.9837651,0.06189333,-0.1681181\" scale = \"3.465945,3.465945,3.465945\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"0.05851394,-0.3096198,3.306754\"
      rotation = \"-0.1691589,0.8265702,-0.3306047,-0.4229272\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Gr\xE0cies a aix\xF2, les eines i les armes
      deixen de ser un privilegi de l\u2019elit: els agricultors tamb\xE9 comencen
      a tenir acc\xE9s a un bon equipament per al seu treball diari.</ca><en>Thanks
      to it, tools and weapons stop being a privilege of the elite: farmers too begin
      to have access to good equipment for their daily work.</en><es>Gracias a ello,
      las herramientas y las armas dejan de ser un privilegio de la \xE9lite: tambi\xE9n
      los agricultores empiezan a tener acceso a buen equipo para su trabajo diario.</es><fr>Gr\xE2ce
      \xE0 cela, les outils et les armes cessent d\u2019\xEAtre un privil\xE8ge r\xE9serv\xE9
      \xE0 l\u2019\xE9lite : les agriculteurs aussi commencent \xE0 avoir acc\xE8s
      \xE0 un bon \xE9quipement pour leur travail quotidien.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>7.296</en><es>9.48</es><fr>9.576</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"2\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>EL
      TRESOR DE LLAVORS\xCD</ca><en>THE LLAVORS\xCD HOARD</en><es>EL TESORO DE LLAVORS\xCD</es><fr>LE
      TR\xC9SOR DES LLAVORS\xCD</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>L\u2019any 1985 es va
      descobrir a prop de Llavors\xED un tresor ocult de 148 peces de bronze, dissimulat
      deliberadament entre roques.</ca><en>In 1985, a hidden hoard of 148 bronze
      pieces was discovered near Llavors\xED, deliberately concealed among rocks</en><es>En
      1985, se descubri\xF3 cerca de Llavors\xED un tesoro oculto de 148 piezas de
      bronce, deliberadamente escondido entre rocas</es><fr>En 1985, un tr\xE9sor
      cach\xE9 de 148 pi\xE8ces de bronze a \xE9t\xE9 d\xE9couvert pr\xE8s de Llavors\xED,
      dissimul\xE9 d\xE9lib\xE9r\xE9ment parmi des rochers</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>8.784</en><es>9.36</es><fr>9.648</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Blacksmith_01\" position = \"-1.771167,0.02666571,4.37816\" rotation
      = \"0.1218685,-0.003509772,0.0004309456,0.99254\" scale = \"0.4616561,0.4616561,0.4616561\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/><asset name = \"Blacksmith_02\"
      position = \"-1.975468,0.02468568,2.19261\" rotation = \"-0.0164996,0.9815306,-0.09970021,-0.1624356\"
      scale = \"0.458865,0.458865,0.458865\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>En aquell moment, el bronze
      era un material valu\xF3s que es podia fondre i reutilitzar una i altra vegada.</ca><en>At
      the time, bronze was a valuable material that could be melted down and reused
      again and again</en><es>En ese momento, el bronce era un material valioso que
      pod\xEDa fundirse y reutilizarse una y otra vez</es><fr>\xC0 l\u2019\xE9poque,
      le bronze \xE9tait un mat\xE9riau pr\xE9cieux que l\u2019on pouvait faire fondre
      et r\xE9utiliser encore et encore</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language
      (ca)</ca><en>6.336</en><es>6.408</es><fr>6.72</fr></audios></token><token id
      = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Per aquest motiu, els
      experts creuen que alg\xFA va amagar aquest petit tresor amb la intenci\xF3
      de recuperar-lo m\xE9s tard, probablement cap al final del segle VIII aC.</ca><en>For
      this reason, experts believe someone hid this small treasure with the intention
      of retrieving it later, likely toward the end of the 8th century BC.</en><es>Por
      esta raz\xF3n, los expertos creen que alguien ocult\xF3 este peque\xF1o tesoro
      con la intenci\xF3n de recuperarlo m\xE1s tarde, probablemente hacia el final
      del siglo VIII a. C.</es><fr>Pour cette raison, des experts pensent que quelqu\u2019un
      a cach\xE9 ce petit tr\xE9sor dans l\u2019intention de le r\xE9cup\xE9rer plus
      tard, probablement vers la fin du VIIIe si\xE8cle av. J.-C.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>7.872</en><es>10.008</es><fr>10.464</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Rings\" position = \"-2.768711,0.6306664,3.229929\" rotation = \"-0.04974786,-0.6089492,-0.03831181,0.7907201\"
      scale = \"3.465647,3.465647,3.465647\" type = \"Video\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration
      id = \"3\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>EMP\xDARIES,
      UNA COL\xD2NIA GREGa</ca><en>EMP\xDARIES, A GREEK COLONY</en><es>EMP\xDARIES,
      UNA COLONIA GRIEGA</es><fr>EMP\xDARIES, UNE COLONIE GRECQUE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Cap al 600 aC, mariners
      foc\xE8us de Mass\xE0lia (Marseille) van fundar Emp\xF2rion. El poblament es
      va establir primer en un petit t\xF3mbol: l\u2019actual Sant Mart\xED d\u2019Emp\xFAries.</ca><en>Around
      600 BC, Phocaean sailors from Massalia (Marseille) founded Emporion. The settlement
      was first established on a small tombolo \u2014 present-day Sant Mart\xED d'Emp\xFAries</en><es>Alrededor
      del 600 a. C., marineros foceos de Massalia (Marsella) fundaron Emporion. El
      asentamiento se estableci\xF3 por primera vez en un peque\xF1o t\xF3mbolo,
      es decir, el actual Sant Mart\xED d'Emp\xFAries</es><fr>Vers 600 av. J.-C.,
      des marins phoc\xE9ens de Massalia (Marseille) fond\xE8rent Emporion. L\u2019\xE9tablissement
      fut d\u2019abord \xE9tabli sur un petit tombolo \u2014 l\u2019actuelle Sant
      Mart\xED d\u2019Emp\xFAries</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>11.28</en><es>12.816</es><fr>11.28</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"True\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>M\xE9s tard, van construir
      una petita ciutat fortificada a la costa continental, al costat d\u2019un port
      natural. Emporion, que en grec significa \xABmercat\xBB, era un port obert
      a mariners de proced\xE8ncies molt diverses.</ca><en>Later, they built a small
      fortified city on the mainland, next to a natural harbor. Emporion, which in
      Greek means \"market,\" was a port open to sailors from the most diverse origins</en><es>M\xE1s
      tarde, construyeron una peque\xF1a ciudad fortificada en el continente, junto
      a un puerto natural. Emporion, que en griego significa \xABmercado\xBB, era
      un puerto abierto a marineros de los or\xEDgenes m\xE1s diversos</es><fr>Plus
      tard, ils construisirent une petite ville fortifi\xE9e sur le continent, \xE0
      c\xF4t\xE9 d\u2019un port naturel. Emporion, qui en grec signifie \xAB march\xE9
      \xBB, \xE9tait un port ouvert aux marins venus des origines les plus diverses</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>11.4</en><es>11.832</es><fr>12.312</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"RuinasEmpuries\" position = \"-4.782421,0.3590564,2.032661\" rotation
      = \"0.0001555512,0.999545,-0.005233688,0.02970762\" scale = \"3.464303,3.464303,3.464303\"
      type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-5.883521,-0.6380843,2.615325\"
      rotation = \"-0.0788959,0.9204344,-0.2518028,-0.2883943\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\"
      type = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>L\u2019assentament original va cr\xE9ixer
      fins a convertir-se en una polis que va arribar a controlar un territori ampli.
      Emp\xFAries va tenir un paper decisiu en la transformaci\xF3 cultural de les
      societats ind\xEDgenes i va servir com a porta d\u2019entrada de la cultura
      cl\xE0ssica a la Pen\xEDnsula Ib\xE8rica.</ca><en>The original settlement grew
      into a polis that came to control a wide territory. Emp\xFAries played a decisive
      role in the cultural transformation of the indigenous societies and served
      as a gateway for classical culture into the Iberian Peninsula</en><es>El asentamiento
      original creci\xF3 hasta convertirse en una polis que lleg\xF3 a controlar
      un amplio territorio. Emp\xFAries desempe\xF1\xF3 un papel decisivo en la transformaci\xF3n
      cultural de las sociedades ind\xEDgenas y sirvi\xF3 como puerta de entrada
      para la cultura cl\xE1sica en la pen\xEDnsula ib\xE9rica</es><fr>L\u2019\xE9tablissement
      d\u2019origine s\u2019est d\xE9velopp\xE9 en une polis qui est parvenue \xE0
      contr\xF4ler un vaste territoire. Emp\xFAries a jou\xE9 un r\xF4le d\xE9cisif
      dans la transformation culturelle des soci\xE9t\xE9s indig\xE8nes et a servi
      de porte d\u2019entr\xE9e \xE0 la culture classique dans la p\xE9ninsule Ib\xE9rique</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>13.848</en><es>15.456</es><fr>15</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-6.691518,-0.5092719,3.966305\" rotation =
      \"0.1586171,-0.7003711,0.1642709,0.6762662\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"4\" startEvent
      = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>UNA CULTURA MEDITERR\xC0NIA</ca><en>A
      MEDITERRANEAN CULTURE</en><es>UNA CULTURA MEDITERR\xC1NEA</es><fr>UNE CULTURE
      M\xC9DITERRAN\xC9ENNE</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Els ibers van mantenir
      el contacte amb altres societats mediterr\xE0nies. A trav\xE9s dels mercats
      p\xFAnics d\u2019Eivissa, van arribar tota mena de productes procedents del
      nord d\u2019\xC0frica.</ca><en>The Iberians maintained contact with other Mediterranean
      societies. Through the Punic markets of Ibiza, all kinds of products arrived
      from North Africa.</en><es>Los \xEDberos mantuvieron el contacto con otras
      sociedades mediterr\xE1neas. A trav\xE9s de los mercados p\xFAnicos de Ibiza,
      llegaron todo tipo de productos desde el norte de \xC1frica.</es><fr>Les Ib\xE8res
      maintenaient des contacts avec d\u2019autres soci\xE9t\xE9s m\xE9diterran\xE9ennes.
      Par les march\xE9s puniques d\u2019Ibiza, toutes sortes de produits arrivaient
      d\u2019Afrique du Nord.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>8.256</en><es>9.288</es><fr>8.16</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>D\u2019Emp\xFAries i Roses,
      els grecs van comerciar amb fines peces de cer\xE0mica de l\u2019\xC0tica i
      del sud d\u2019It\xE0lia. Tamb\xE9 hi havia relacions d\u2019influ\xE8ncia
      amb el m\xF3n gal.</ca><en>From Emp\xFAries and Roses, the Greeks traded fine
      ceramic wares from Attica and southern Italy. There were also relationships
      of influence with the Gallic world. </en><es>Desde Emp\xFAries y Rosas, los
      griegos comerciaban con vajillas de cer\xE1mica fina de \xC1tica y del sur
      de Italia. Tambi\xE9n exist\xEDan relaciones de influencia con el mundo galo.</es><fr>Depuis
      Emp\xFAries et Roses, les Grecs commer\xE7aient des poteries de qualit\xE9
      venant de l\u2019Attique et de l\u2019Italie du Sud. Il existait aussi des
      relations d\u2019influence avec le monde gaulois.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>9.48</en><es>9.96</es><fr>9.24</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Anfora\" position = \"-0.859252,0.2613881,11.27649\" rotation = \"0.02966494,-0.008737096,0.0002593095,0.9995217\"
      scale = \"3.466139,3.466139,3.466139\" type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"0.026757,-0.8236305,10.63194\" rotation =
      \"0.3048611,0.2629707,-0.0879888,0.9111335\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type =
      \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token><token id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\" pause
      = \"False\"><languages><ca>Entre els molts pobles ibers que vivien en el que
      avui \xE9s Catalunya, els de les zones costaneres mostren un desenvolupament
      urb\xE0, econ\xF2mic i cultural remarcable, mentre que els grups de l\u2019interior
      depenien principalment de l\u2019agricultura i la ramaderia.</ca><en>Among
      the many Iberian peoples living in what is now Catalonia, those in the coastal
      areas show remarkable urban, economic, and cultural development, while inland
      groups relied predominantly on farming and livestock.</en><es>Entre los muchos
      pueblos ib\xE9ricos que viv\xEDan en lo que hoy es Catalu\xF1a, los de las
      zonas costeras muestran un desarrollo urbano, econ\xF3mico y cultural notable,
      mientras que los grupos del interior depend\xEDan predominantemente de la agricultura
      y la ganader\xEDa.</es><fr>Parmi les nombreux peuples ib\xE8res vivant dans
      ce qui est aujourd\u2019hui la Catalogne, ceux des r\xE9gions c\xF4ti\xE8res
      pr\xE9sentent un d\xE9veloppement urbain, \xE9conomique et culturel remarquable,
      tandis que les groupes de l\u2019int\xE9rieur reposaient principalement sur
      l\u2019agriculture et l\u2019\xE9levage.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for
      language (ca)</ca><en>12.096</en><es>13.296</es><fr>14.184</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Waypoint\" position = \"-1.722066,-0.7899158,10.63139\" rotation =
      \"0.2942372,-0.2750557,0.08884063,0.9109754\" scale = \"0.2,0.2,0.2\" type
      = \"Waypoints\" animation = \"\"/></token></narration><narration id = \"5\"
      startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id = \"0\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>MOLINS ROTATORIS</ca><en>ROTARY
      MILLS</en><es>MOLINOS ROTATORIOS</es><fr>MOULINS ROTATIFS</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Moldre el gra fins a convertir-lo
      en farina sempre ha estat una feina feixuga. Des del Neol\xEDtic, s\u2019han
      utilitzat molins de vaiv\xE9, per\xF2 a partir del segle V aC van comen\xE7ar
      a apar\xE8ixer els molins rotatoris, inventats per les comunitats ib\xE8riques
      que vivien a l\u2019actual Catalunya.</ca><en>Grinding grain into flour has
      always been hard work. Since the Neolithic, saddle querns were used, but starting
      in the 5th century BC, rotary mills began to appear, invented by the Iberian
      communities living in what is now Catalonia. </en><es>Molerse el grano hasta
      convertirlo en harina siempre ha sido un trabajo duro. Desde el Neol\xEDtico
      se usaron muelas de vaiv\xE9n, pero a partir del siglo V a. C. empezaron a
      aparecer los molinos rotatorios, inventados por las comunidades iberas que
      viv\xEDan en lo que hoy es Catalu\xF1a.</es><fr>R\xE9duire le grain en farine
      a toujours \xE9t\xE9 un travail difficile. Depuis le N\xE9olithique, on utilisait
      des meules \xE0 sellette, mais \xE0 partir du Ve si\xE8cle av. J.-C., des moulins
      rotatifs ont commenc\xE9 \xE0 appara\xEEtre, invent\xE9s par les communaut\xE9s
      ib\xE9riques vivant dans ce qui est aujourd\u2019hui la Catalogne.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>16.32</en><es>16.272</es><fr>16.536</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Carpenter\" position = \"0.9596153,0.1224091,10.24739\" rotation =
      \"-0.001688835,0.9975739,-0.06451015,-0.02611585\" scale = \"0.5461183,0.5461183,0.5461183\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token id = \"1\" audioclip
      = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\" destroy = \"False\"
      pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>La seva operaci\xF3 era simple: el gra s\u2019abocava
      a trav\xE9s d\u2019un forat a la pedra superior, que girava contra la pedra
      inferior, aixafant-la fins a convertir-la en farina.</ca><en>Their operation
      was simple: grain was poured through a hole in the upper stone, which turned
      against the lower stone, crushing it into flour. </en><es>Su operaci\xF3n era
      sencilla: se vert\xEDa grano a trav\xE9s de un orificio en la piedra superior,
      que giraba contra la piedra inferior, tritur\xE1ndola hasta convertirla en
      harina.</es><fr>Leur op\xE9ration \xE9tait simple : on versait le grain \xE0
      travers un trou dans la pierre sup\xE9rieure, qui tournait contre la pierre
      inf\xE9rieure, la broyant en farine.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language
      (ca)</ca><en>7.92</en><es>9.864</es><fr>8.544</fr></audios><asset name = \"MolinoGris,MolinoOlson\"
      position = \"1.942974,0.4777002,11.35573\" rotation = \"-0.01675617,0.727554,0.01778113,0.6856152\"
      scale = \"3.464379,3.464379,3.464379\" type = \"Image\" animation = \"\"/></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>Aquesta invenci\xF3 es
      va estendre juntament amb l\u2019arribada d\u2019eines de ferro, que permetien
      treballar la terra de manera m\xE9s eficient.</ca><en>This invention spread
      alongside the arrival of iron tools, which allowed the land to be worked more
      efficiently.</en><es>Esta invenci\xF3n se extendi\xF3 junto con la llegada
      de herramientas de hierro, que permitieron trabajar la tierra de manera m\xE1s
      eficiente.</es><fr>Cette invention s\u2019est r\xE9pandue avec l\u2019arriv\xE9e
      des outils en fer, qui ont permis de travailler la terre plus efficacement.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>5.52</en><es>7.2</es><fr>6.24</fr></audios></token></narration><narration
      id = \"6\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" title=\"nothing\"><title id =
      \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\"><languages><ca>UN
      PETIT VAIXELL ROM\xC0</ca><en>A SMALL ROMAN SHIP</en><es>UN PEQUE\xD1O BARCO
      ROMANO</es><fr>UN PETIT NAVIRE ROMAIN</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en></en><es></es><fr></fr></audios></title><token
      id = \"0\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>El Culip IV \xE9s un petit
      vaixell rom\xE0 que es va enfonsar entre el 70 i el 80 aC a la cala del Culip,
      a prop del cap de Creus. Es va proveir de productes agr\xEDcoles i manufacturats
      d\u2019or\xEDgens diversos, arribant a ports importants com Narbo (Narbonne),
      i va transportar aquesta c\xE0rrega de tornada a pobles al llarg de la costa
      catalana situats fora de les principals rutes directes de distribuci\xF3.</ca><en>Culip
      IV is a small Roman ship that sank between 70 and 80 BC in the Culip cove,
      near Cape Creus. It stocked up on agricultural and manufactured goods from
      various origins, arriving at major ports such as Narbo (Narbonne), and carried
      this cargo back to towns along the Catalan coast located outside the main direct
      distribution routes.</en><es>El Culip IV es un peque\xF1o barco romano que
      se hundi\xF3 entre el 70 y el 80 a. C. en la cala de Culip, cerca del cabo
      de Creus. Se aprovision\xF3 de productos agr\xEDcolas y manufacturados de diversos
      or\xEDgenes, llegando a grandes puertos como Narbo (Narbonne), y transport\xF3
      esta carga de regreso a poblaciones a lo largo de la costa catalana situadas
      fuera de las principales rutas directas de distribuci\xF3n.</es><fr>Culip IV
      est un petit navire romain qui a coul\xE9 entre 70 et 80 av. J.-C. dans la
      crique de Culip, pr\xE8s du cap de Creus. Il s\u2019approvisionnait en produits
      agricoles et manufactur\xE9s provenant de diverses origines, en faisant escale
      dans de grands ports tels que Narbo (Narbonne), et transportait cette cargaison
      vers des villes situ\xE9es le long de la c\xF4te catalane, en dehors des principaux
      itin\xE9raires de distribution directs.</fr></languages><audios><ca></ca><en>22.296</en><es>22.968</es><fr>23.52</fr></audios><asset
      name = \"Merchant_01\" position = \"3.688454,0.8094716,8.249096\" rotation
      = \"-0.1079199,0.03816688,0.004146259,0.993418\" scale = \"0.6008493,0.6008493,0.6008493\"
      type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Talking\"/><asset name = \"Merchant_02\" position
      = \"4.500345,0.7821566,8.008343\" rotation = \"-0.09774859,0.2524615,0.02564414,0.9623153\"
      scale = \"0.6058975,0.6058975,0.6058975\" type = \"Model3D\" animation = \"Pointing\"/></token><token
      id = \"1\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>La c\xE0rrega documentada
      \xE9s molt diversa, incloent-hi al voltant de 80 \xE0mfores d\u2019oli de B\xE8tica,
      vaixella de taula produ\xEFda a G\xE0l\xB7lia i a B\xE8tica, i ll\xE0nties
      d\u2019oli fetes a Roma. Tamb\xE9 hi ha un nombre redu\xEFt d\u2019\xE0mfores
      d\u2019or\xEDgens diversos que transportaven vi i peix salat.</ca><en>The documented
      cargo is highly varied, including around 80 amphorae of oil from Baetica, tableware
      produced in Gaul and Baetica, and oil lamps made in Rome. There is also a small
      number of amphorae of various origins that carried wine and salted fish. </en><es>La
      carga documentada es sumamente variada e incluye alrededor de 80 \xE1nforas
      de aceite de la B\xE9tica, vajilla producida en la Galia y la B\xE9tica, y
      l\xE1mparas de aceite fabricadas en Roma. Tambi\xE9n hay un peque\xF1o n\xFAmero
      de \xE1nforas de diversos or\xEDgenes que transportaban vino y pescado salado.</es><fr>La
      cargaison document\xE9e est tr\xE8s vari\xE9e, comprenant environ 80 amphores
      d\u2019huile de B\xE9tique, de la vaisselle produite en Gaule et en B\xE9tique,
      ainsi que des lampes \xE0 huile fabriqu\xE9es \xE0 Rome. Il y a \xE9galement
      un petit nombre d\u2019amphores de diverses origines qui transportaient du
      vin et du poisson sal\xE9.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text for language (ca)</ca><en>15.072</en><es>15.984</es><fr>15.12</fr></audios></token><token
      id = \"2\" audioclip = \"\" startEvent = \"\" endEvent = \"\" hide = \"False\"
      destroy = \"False\" pause = \"False\"><languages><ca>La c\xE0rrega recuperada
      permet estimar la mida del vaixell: una embarcaci\xF3 petita de menys de 11
      m de longitud, amb una m\xE0nega d\u2019uns 3 m.</ca><en>The recovered cargo
      makes it possible to estimate the size of the ship: a small vessel under 11
      m in length, with a beam of about 3 m.</en><es>La carga recuperada permite
      estimar el tama\xF1o del barco: una embarcaci\xF3n peque\xF1a de menos de 11
      m de longitud, con una manga de aproximadamente 3 m.</es><fr>La cargaison r\xE9cup\xE9r\xE9e
      permet d\u2019estimer la taille du navire : un petit b\xE2timent de moins de
      11 m de longueur, avec une largeur d\u2019environ 3 m.</fr></languages><audios><ca>Text
      for language (ca)</ca><en>9.048</en><es>9.192</es><fr>8.304</fr></audios></token></narration></narrations>"
